#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator skala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial implements a [Qiskit pattern](/guides/intro-to-patterns) to "
"simulate a one-dimensional (1D) Many-Body Localization (MBL) circuit. The "
"MBL circuit is a hardware-efficient circuit and is parameterized by two "
"parameters $\\theta$ and $\\vec{\\phi}$. When $\\theta$ is set to $0$ and "
"the initial state is prepared in $|0\\rangle$ for all the qubits, the ideal "
"expectation value of $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ is $+1$ for every qubit site "
"$i$ irrespective of the values of $\\vec{\\phi}$. More details on this "
"circuit are available in this "
"[article](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-57623-x).\n"
msgstr ""
"Tutorial ini melaksanakan [corak Qiskit](/guides/intro-to-patterns) untuk "
"mensimulasikan litar Many-Body Localization (MBL) satu dimensi (1D). Litar "
"MBL ialah litar yang cekap dari segi perkakasan dan diparameterkan oleh dua "
"parameter $\\theta$ dan $\\vec{\\phi}$. Apabila $\\theta$ ditetapkan kepada "
"$0$ dan keadaan awal disediakan dalam $|0\\rangle$ untuk semua qubit, nilai "
"jangkaan ideal bagi $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ ialah $+1$ untuk setiap tapak "
"qubit $i$ tanpa mengira nilai $\\vec{\\phi}$. Butiran lanjut tentang litar "
"ini tersedia dalam "
"[artikel](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-57623-x) ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that in a noiseless simulator, the expectation value obtained with and "
"without circuit cutting will be same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu diingat bahawa dalam simulator tanpa hingar, nilai jangkaan yang "
"diperoleh dengan dan tanpa pemotongan litar adalah sama.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-"
"classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Construct the 1D MBL circuit {#construct-the-1d-mbl-circuit}"
msgstr "Bina litar MBL 1D {#construct-the-1d-mbl-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "First, we present a function for constructing the 1D MBL circuit.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita kemukakan fungsi untuk membina litar MBL 1D.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/a3debf65-06df-4277-933e-14b6f6170756-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/a3debf65-06df-4277-933e-14b6f6170756-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We calculate the average expectation value $O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_i Z_i$ "
"over all qubits for $\\theta = 0$. Since the ideal expectation value of "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle = 1$ $\\forall$ $i$, the ideal expectation value of "
"$O$ is also $1$. The parameters $\\phi$ are selected randomly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mengira nilai jangkaan purata $O = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_i Z_i$ ke atas "
"semua qubit untuk $\\theta = 0$. Oleh kerana nilai jangkaan ideal bagi "
"$\\langle Z_i \\rangle = 1$ $\\forall$ $i$, nilai jangkaan ideal bagi $O$ "
"juga ialah $1$. Parameter $\\phi$ dipilih secara rawak.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit needs to be annotated by inserting **CutWire** in the desired "
"locations to partition it. For this tutorial, we opt for equal partition. "
"The MBL circuit is designed so that setting `use_cut=True` in the function "
"inserts the annotation properly after $\\frac{n}{2}$ qubits, $n$ being the "
"number of qubits in the original circuit. We also assigned the randomly "
"generated parameters to the circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar perlu ditandakan dengan memasukkan **CutWire** di lokasi yang "
"dikehendaki untuk mempartisinya. Untuk tutorial ini, kita memilih partition "
"yang sama rata. Litar MBL direka bentuk supaya menetapkan `use_cut=True` "
"dalam fungsi akan memasukkan tanda dengan betul selepas $\\frac{n}{2}$ "
"qubit, dengan $n$ ialah bilangan qubit dalam litar asal. Kita juga "
"menetapkan parameter yang dijana secara rawak kepada litar tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/5208e0a8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/5208e0a8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cut the circuit into smaller subcircuits {#cut-the-circuit-into-smaller-"
"subcircuits}"
msgstr ""
"Potong litar kepada subLitar yang lebih kecil {#cut-the-circuit-into-"
"smaller-subcircuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we partition the circuit into two smaller subcircuits using [`qiskit-"
"addon-cutting`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/). `qiskit-"
"addon-cutting` appends a virtual `Move` gate to split the wire cut location "
"by appropriately adjusting the number of qubits. Now we create the circuit "
"with this virtual gate. Since there is one wire cut, the number of "
"associated qubits will be increased by 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita partisi litar kepada dua subLitar yang lebih kecil menggunakan"
" [`qiskit-addon-cutting`](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-cutting/). "
"`qiskit-addon-cutting` menambahkan gerbang `Move` maya untuk memisahkan "
"lokasi pemotongan wayar dengan menyesuaikan bilangan qubit dengan "
"sewajarnya. Sekarang kita cipta litar dengan gerbang maya ini. Oleh kerana "
"terdapat satu pemotongan wayar, bilangan qubit yang berkaitan akan ditambah "
"sebanyak 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1834cb22-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1834cb22-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Construct and expand the observable {#construct-and-expand-the-observable}"
msgstr ""
"Bina dan kembangkan pemerhatian {#construct-and-expand-the-observable}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The observable, as defined before, will be the average of $Z$ on each qubit."
" However, upon inserting the virtual `Move` gate, the effective number of "
"qubits in the circuit increases. The observable must also be expanded "
"accordingly to account for this change in the number of qubits. Note the "
"observable always acts trivially (as in $I$) on the extra qubit added for "
"the virtual `Move` gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pemerhatian, seperti yang ditakrifkan sebelum ini, ialah purata $Z$ pada "
"setiap qubit. Walau bagaimanapun, setelah memasukkan gerbang `Move` maya, "
"bilangan qubit efektif dalam litar bertambah. Pemerhatian juga mesti "
"dikembangkan mengikutnya untuk mengambil kira perubahan dalam bilangan qubit"
" ini. Perlu diingat bahawa pemerhatian sentiasa bertindak secara trivial "
"(seperti $I$) pada qubit tambahan yang ditambah untuk gerbang `Move` maya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now the circuit can be partitioned along the `Move` gate and we obtain the "
"subcircuits, as well as the subobservable, which is the portion of the "
"original observable associated with each subcircuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang litar boleh dipartisi mengikut gerbang `Move` dan kita memperoleh "
"subLitar, serta subPemerhatian, iaitu bahagian pemerhatian asal yang "
"berkaitan dengan setiap subLitar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Here we visualize the two subcircuits:\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita visualisasikan dua subLitar:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1b0e779f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/1b0e779f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/3c802f28-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/wire-"
"cutting/extracted-outputs/3c802f28-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Expanding the observable using the `Move` operation requires a `PauliList` "
"data structure. To reconstruct the expectation value of the original "
"circuit, we require the observable in the `SparsePauliOp` format.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mengembangkan pemerhatian menggunakan operasi `Move` memerlukan struktur "
"data `PauliList`. Untuk merekonstruksi nilai jangkaan litar asal, kita "
"memerlukan pemerhatian dalam format `SparsePauliOp`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As discussed before, for each cut the upstream circuit must be measured in a"
" Pauli basis, and the downstream circuit must be prepared in the eigenstate "
"of the basis. The function `generate_cutting_experiments` creates all of "
"these necessary circuits and the coefficients associated with each circuit "
"required for reconstruction. Find more detail in [this "
"paper](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.150504).\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti yang dibincangkan sebelum ini, untuk setiap pemotongan litar "
"upstream mesti diukur dalam basis Pauli, dan litar downstream mesti "
"disediakan dalam eigenstate basis tersebut. Fungsi "
"`generate_cutting_experiments` mencipta semua litar yang diperlukan ini "
"beserta pekali yang berkaitan dengan setiap litar yang diperlukan untuk "
"rekonstruksi. Cari butiran lanjut dalam [kertas kerja "
"ini](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.125.150504).\n"

